scripture: Matthew 7:14; Matthew 7:7-8

=== Rejected
--- Opposed the truth
scripture: 2 Timothy 3:8; 2 Thessalonians 2:11-12

--- God gave them up
scripture: Romans 1:21-26

=== Received or rejected
--- The gift of righteousness
lead: God would all choose the gift of righteousness through the sacrifice of Christ, washed in His blood, the sole propitiation for our sin.
p: The gift of eternal salvation has been received by faith, calling upon the name of the Lord, since Seth. Those who willingly come to accept salvation are written in the book of life of the Lamb, slain from the foundation of the World. Those who don't before they die, erased.

--- Made reprobate
lead: Those who, while living willfully reject the gift, eventually are made reprobate, cast off, turned over and rejected by God and given what they want; to no longer retain God in their knowledge.
p: Their conscience seared. Sons of Belial. Dogs, twice dead. Filled with all unrighteousness and burning with unnatural lusts, for sins not common to mankind. Enemies of God. Antichrists. Deserving death.

--- Received, or rejected [title]
heading: Received, or rejected
point: Received | The gift of eternal salvation has been received by faith, calling upon the name of the Lord, since Seth.
point: Rejected | Those who, while living willfully reject the gift, eventually are made reprobate.
